  "summary": "New preprints probe what scGPT, Cell2Sentence and STATE learn and benchmark five single-cell foundation models against simple baselines.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is scrutiny of what single-cell models learn and when they add value. A post-hoc attribution study dissects scGPT, Cell2Sentence and STATE across cell annotation and perturbation prediction. A separate benchmark pits five single-cell foundation models against simple baselines for annotation, in silico perturbation and GRN inference, reporting that they help mainly in specific settings. Several methods build interpretability into the architecture. irAEGIS uses a pathway-guided hierarchical model to predict immune-related adverse events from pre-treatment scRNA-seq. scCont pairs contrastive learning with Shapley attribution on an EMT timecourse. scDisentangle generates identity-preserving counterfactuals for perturbation response. ExPert inverts the perturbation problem, inferring causal perturbations from observed cell states via latent prototypes across 12 contexts. Agentic systems (CellCanon, LabWeaver, SSAF-T) emphasize evidence-grounded explanation and grounding in laboratory knowledge. What is new is treating explainability and comparison against simple baselines as first-class evaluation criteria rather than reporting accuracy alone.",
